Heeler: start the metrics saver thread only while metrics are written.

ZeroTierOne 1.16 links prometheus-cpp-lite's SaveToFile as a global
(prometheus::simpleapi::saver in node/Metrics.cpp). Its thread starts with
the object, during static initialization, so in any process that links
libzt from launch on, whether or not ZeroTier is ever used; it wakes every
1/100 of its period (10 ms by default, 100 ms once libzt's NodeService
lengthens it) to check for work, even with no registry to save. Heeler
never enables metrics (zts_init_enable_metrics), so that thread only costs
wakeups on a phone.

This patch changes SaveToFile (core/include/prometheus/save_to_file.h):
- no thread at construction; set_registry with a registry starts it,
  set_registry without one stops it (after a last save, as stopping did);
- the thread sleeps on a condition variable for the whole period and is
  woken at once to stop, instead of polling;
- period, file name, and registry are guarded by a mutex.

libzt's zts_init_enable_metrics still works: NodeService sets the registry
when metrics are enabled and clears it when the node stops. The changed
file carries a "Modified by Heeler contributors" notice.

Applies to ZeroTierOne fc5c3ec22090b5b2a0f274e863651fe9ca489bf4 (1.16.2) in
libzt's ext/ZeroTierOne (ext/prometheus-cpp-lite-1.0 only).

